@startuml
title Phone-side see paired watches and remote logout management

actor User

participant SettingPage as "<color:white>SettingPage</color>" #darkgreen
'participant ConnectedWatchesPage as "<color:white>ConnectedWatchesPage</color>" #darkgreen
participant UserController as "<color:white>UserController</color>" #151b8e
participant AuthService as "<color:white>AuthService</color>" #000000
participant FirebaseAuth
database FirebaseFirestore

User -> SettingPage : tap "Managed Paired Watches"

SettingPage -> UserController : getConnectedWatches()
UserController -> AuthService : getConnectedWatches()

AuthService -> FirebaseAuth : currentUser
FirebaseAuth --> AuthService : user

    AuthService -> FirebaseFirestore : collection("watch_pair").where("uid", isEqualTo: user.uid).where("status", isEqualTo: "approved").get()
    FirebaseFirestore --> AuthService : snap
    AuthService --> UserController : List<Map<String,dynamic>>
    UserController --> SettingPage : connected watches
    SettingPage --> User : show connected watches list




note right of SettingPage
The page shows the watches that are currently paired
with the authenticated phone user according to the
live state stored in the watch_pair collection.
It is therefore a view of the current pairing state,
not a historical registry of all watches ever used.
end note

opt Enable remote logout for a selected watch
    User -> SettingPage : tap "Enable remote logout"
    SettingPage -> UserController : enableRemoteLogoutForWatch(watchId)
    UserController -> AuthService : enableRemoteLogoutForWatch(watchId)

    AuthService -> FirebaseAuth : currentUser
    FirebaseAuth --> AuthService : user / null



       
        AuthService -> FirebaseFirestore : collection("watch_pair").doc(watchId).update({"remoteLogoutAt": serverTimestamp()})
        FirebaseFirestore --> AuthService : update completed
        AuthService --> UserController : success
        UserController --> SettingPage : success
        ref over SettingPage, UserController, AuthService, FirebaseAuth, FirebaseFirestore : reload watches through getConnectedWatches()
        SettingPage --> User : show remote logout enabled

end

opt Disable remote logout for a selected watch
    User -> SettingPage : tap "Disable remote logout"
    SettingPage -> UserController : clearRemoteLogoutForWatch(watchId)
    UserController -> AuthService : clearRemoteLogoutForWatch(watchId)

    AuthService -> FirebaseAuth : currentUser
    FirebaseAuth --> AuthService : user / null

    
        AuthService -> FirebaseFirestore : collection("watch_pair").doc(watchId).update({"remoteLogoutAt": null})
        FirebaseFirestore --> AuthService : update completed
        AuthService --> UserController : success
        UserController --> SettingPage : success
        ref over SettingPage, UserController, AuthService, FirebaseAuth, FirebaseFirestore : reload watches through getConnectedWatches()
        SettingPage --> User : show remote logout cleared
   
end

note left of FirebaseFirestore
The remote logout flag does not replace the ordinary
pairing protocol. It is an additional control field
written only by the phone. The watch-side reaction
is handled by the listener already observing the
same watch_pair document.
end note

@enduml